From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:08:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix numpy.i for SWIG >=4.3's 3-arg SWIG_Python_AppendOutput

SWIG 4.3.0 added an `is_void` third parameter to its generated
SWIG_Python_AppendOutput() runtime helper (pyrun.swg). xtgeo's own
project-local src/lib/numpy.i still calls it with the pre-4.3 two-arg
form in every ARGOUT_ARRAY* typemap, so building with any SWIG >=4.3
fails with "too few arguments to function 'SWIG_Python_AppendOutput'"
-- reproduces on any arch, this host included.

Pass is_void=0 at every call site. That is the behaviour-preserving
value: pyrun.swg's is_void only changes behaviour when $result is
Py_None, by skipping the list-wrapping branch so a void primary return
is replaced outright instead of turned into a list; the pre-4.3
two-arg function always took the list-wrapping branch, which is what
is_void=0 reproduces.

This is required independently of which SWIG >=4.3 is used: swig<4.3
has no riscv64 wheel on PyPI (gotcha territory -- see the companion
0001 patch, which drops that pin), and 4.3.1.post0 (the first riscv64
release) hits this same error.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 needs SWIG>=4.3.1.post0 for a PyPI wheel; this project-local numpy.i was never updated for SWIG 4.3's runtime signature change]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 src/lib/numpy.i | 76 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------------------
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

